    "topic": "**FOSSi Z80** by ReJ (Renaldas Zioma): an open-source, pin compatible replacement for the classic Zilog Z80 8-bit CPU, with chips on wafer.space runs.\n\n**Run 1**\n• [RZ80](https://wafer.space/ws-run1/projects/RZ80.html) (1x1 slot)\n• [HZ80](https://wafer.space/ws-run1/projects/HZ80.html) (0.5x1 slot)\n**Run 2**\n• [HZ80](https://wafer.space/ws-run2/projects/HZ80.html) (0.5x1 slot)\n• [QZ80](https://wafer.space/ws-run2/projects/QZ80.html) (0.5x0.5 slot)\n**Source**\n• [z80-open-silicon](https://github.com/rejunity/z80-open-silicon)\n• [ws0-z80-open-silicon-gf180mcu](https://github.com/rejunity/ws0-z80-open-silicon-gf180mcu)\n**Talks** (project background, from the Tiny Tapeout 07 version)\n• [Slides: Z80 on Tiny Tapeout](https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1-vcqAm9nMe9o_P5PAofOEgkbrVqfZs-Lbs7DuWj7h2o)\n• [Video with Matt Venn](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GI1e22A2J3U)"
